geowarden (1.6.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Blocked networks (BLOCK_NETS): networks or addresses that are always
    blocked, whatever their country. Managed in the new menu entry
    "Blocked networks", or straight from "Top 10 addresses" and the new
    statistics page "Suspicious networks".
  * BLOCK_NETS_OPEN_PORTS chooses whether blocked networks may still use
    the open ports (default: blocked there too).
  * Scanner hint: networks that send requests from many different addresses
    are marked as suspected scanners in the top 10, the new page and the
    live view (IPv4: 8 or more addresses in a /24 or 12 or more in a /22,
    IPv6: 8 or more in a /48).
  * The menu warns before blocking the network of the own SSH connection.

 -- Thomas Marx <103289949+tommx0@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000

