geowarden (1.4.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * geowarden-apply is now written in Python, like the menu (#1). bash, curl
    and gzip are no longer needed.
  * Neighbouring IP ranges of allowed countries are joined before loading:
    about half as many ranges for nft to load, so the daily reload is faster.
    The rules in the kernel stay the same.
  * nft loads the rules once instead of checking them with "nft -c" first:
    "nft -f" is a single transaction that changes nothing if it fails, so
    the check did the same work twice.
  * Every line of the geo data is checked; a damaged cached file is
    downloaded again.
  * The settings in /etc/geowarden.conf are checked (country codes,
    interfaces, ports, STATS_MAX) before any rule is changed.
  * The menu shows version, year, author, license and project page at the
    top of every dialog.

 -- Thomas Marx <103289949+tommx0@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

geowarden (1.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * STATS_MAX in /etc/geowarden.conf limits the addresses per statistics
    list (default 10000, 0 turns the statistics off).
  * Top 10 countries: typing a country code shows the top 10 allowed and
    blocked addresses of that country.

